  "details": "when using the input binding system the application can specify actions, that can be mapped instead of just \"trigger press\", \"touchpad press\", etc...\n\nThis means you can e.g. set the different gestures via that remapping, wich should allow for example index users to set their gestures the way they like to despite VRCs gesture animation system. and therefore the index's and future controller's finger tracking could be implemented easier.\na true input rebinding function has been missing from all VR games i've played until now meaning utilizing that system valve / the openVR guys set up would be a good idea...\n\nalso for further clearance and sorting inputs can be put into tabs inside the remap dialogue. This means there can be a \"General\" tab, a \"Gestures\" tab and maybe more.\n\nEDIT: I dont own index controllers and therefore dont know if finger positions can be remapped, but i bet it is possible and if not, then it will be possible at some point\n\nEDIT2: https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/knucklesindex-controller-support-compressed-skeletal-hand-input this could then be implemented no matter what, by overwriting the skeletal movement with the animations set through the remapping. (at least for the hands. idk about full body skeletal input with normal controllers and trackers..)",
